Subject: [PATCH] Export Protobuf include fragments from Debian packages

Origin: sonic-bazel-registry rules_distroless 0.9.4-sonic.1,
patches/0002-include-fragments.patch.

Protobuf public headers include files such as google/protobuf/port_def.inc.
Distroless 0.9.4 omits these fragments from the imported compilation inputs,
so Bazel's C++ sandbox cannot find them. Preserve the existing SONiC fix by
exporting .inc files under usr/include alongside normal headers.

---
diff --git a/apt/private/deb_import.bzl b/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
--- a/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
@@ -233,7 +233,7 @@
             a_files.append(line)
         elif line.endswith(".pc") and line.find("pkgconfig"):
             pc_files.append(line)
-        elif line.endswith(".h"):
+        elif line.endswith(".h") or (line.startswith("usr/include/") and line.endswith(".inc")):
             h_files.append(line)
         elif line.endswith(".hpp"):
             hpp_files.append(line)
